usage: test_quality_widen_e2e.py [-h] --source SOURCE --output OUTPUT --group
                                 {wide,review-red}
                                 [--case {widen_red_rules_success,red_manifest_missing,red_base_not_failing,red_candidate_fails,red_rules_failing,red_rules_frozen,widen_red_manifest_paths,widen_red_symlink,widen_bad_project_config,widen_abandon,widen_upgrade,widen_ending_invalid_fields,widen_scores_roundtrip,widen_score_before_cas,widen_score_after_cas,reviewer_create_red,reviewer_restart_red,reviewer_reclaim_red}]

Widened quality contracts and explicit reviewer fault probes. Only the owned
daemon is signalled. Git fault windows reuse the independent recovery
fixture's wrapper, read as source data without changing its assertions.

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --source SOURCE
  --output OUTPUT
  --group {wide,review-red}
  --case {widen_red_rules_success,red_manifest_missing,red_base_not_failing,red_candidate_fails,red_rules_failing,red_rules_frozen,widen_red_manifest_paths,widen_red_symlink,widen_bad_project_config,widen_abandon,widen_upgrade,widen_ending_invalid_fields,widen_scores_roundtrip,widen_score_before_cas,widen_score_after_cas,reviewer_create_red,reviewer_restart_red,reviewer_reclaim_red}
